Rewritten from the Python plugin into one Nodecode cell. The original's
plugin_scaffold wrote a Hermes plugin folder -- plugin.yaml, __init__.py,
schemas.py, tools.py -- under ~/.hermes/plugins from a description, and its
plugin_add_tool patched one it had written; that is cell_scaffold and
cell_add_tool here, writing a cell folder for THIS organism instead: the
system and its test system, one cell.lisp carrying the package, a schema and
a handler a tool and the nle:define-cell declaration, a README and the
folder's tests. Its requires_env list became the section fields a generated
cell declares, and its bundled French-language skill became the guide line
the generated cell's section carries, which the setup panel and the model
already read.

Left out, and why:

  * plugin_add_skill. A bundled SKILL.md is a Hermes registry entry; Nodecode
    has none, so the third verb is cell_add_command -- one more slash command
    spliced into a cell -- and the prose a cell carries rides in its section's
    GUIDE line, which the setup panel and the model already read.
  * plugin.yaml, schemas.py and tools.py. A Nodecode cell is an .asd and Lisp
    files; the nle:define-cell declaration is the manifest, so there is
    nothing for a separate manifest to keep in step.
  * The original's name normalization kept dots and slashes, so a name could
    point outside the plugins folder. A name here is letters, digits and
    dashes only, and an existing folder is refused rather than overwritten.
